course: dictionary
lesson: 1818
title: Clunky
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Clunky describes something big, heavy and awkward, not smooth or easy to use. «Grandad's clunky old phone takes ages to open an app.» The phone is not quick or sleek. It is heavy and awkward to use, so clunky means awkward.
explain: The same word can describe writing. «Using a fronted adverbial in every sentence makes writing sound clunky; use them for variety.» A fronted adverbial is a word or phrase at the start of a sentence, like «Later,». Here clunky means the writing reads stiffly and awkwardly, not smoothly.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try "awkward and stiff" in place of clunky. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: «Clunky» means big, heavy and awkward, not smooth or neat to use.
fact: «Clunky» can describe old phones, computers and furniture.
fact: In English lessons, a sentence that reads badly can be called clunky.
fact: The comparative form is clunkier, and the superlative is clunkiest.
exercise: «Grandad's clunky old phone takes ages to open an app.» What does clunky mean here? | Very quiet | *Big, heavy and awkward to use | Bright and shiny
exercise: «Using a fronted adverbial in every sentence makes writing sound clunky; use them for variety.» What does clunky mean in this sentence? | Funny and light | *Awkward and stiff, not smooth to read | Long and colourful
exercise: Which word is the comparative form of clunky? | *clunkier | cluck | clunky
test: «The old computer was so clunky that Ella gave up waiting for it to start.» What does clunky suggest? | Quick and light | *Heavy and awkward to use | Colourful and fun
test: Which sentence best describes a clunky sentence in writing? | *A sentence that reads awkwardly and stiffly | A sentence that reads smoothly | A sentence with no words at all
exam: Ruby says a clunky sentence is one that is short and sweet. Is she right? | Yes, clunky means quick and light | Yes, clunky means short and sweet | *No, clunky means awkward and not smooth to use or read
